<title>USA: Exporters--Taiwan soy sale now optional US origin.</title>
<headline>Exporters--Taiwan soy sale now optional US origin.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exporters said they changed a 108,000-tonne sale of U.S. soybeans to Taiwan for 1996/97 delivery to optional origin, Agriculture Department said Monday.</p>
<p>An optional origin contract allows a commodity to come from the United States or another exporting nation.</p>
<p>Marketing year for soybeans began last Sept 1.</p>
<p>By law, exporters must promptly report all major sales.</p>
</text>
